00:27:09.030 --> 00:27:12.210
that it works hand-in-hand
with BigQuery,

00:27:12.210 --> 00:27:17.070
and Dataproc, and other
data platforms on GCP.

00:27:17.070 --> 00:27:17.880
What does it do?

00:27:17.880 --> 00:27:21.750
It brokers that service directly
into the business applications

00:27:21.750 --> 00:27:24.450
on the integration side.

00:27:24.450 --> 00:27:28.110
So Cloud Pub/Sub is the way
to go for most integration

00:27:28.110 --> 00:27:30.000
scenarios in the GCP world.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.390
We've got the ways of
integrating into that

00:27:32.390 --> 00:27:33.480
at the messaging layer.

00:27:33.480 --> 00:27:37.530
We have enterprise messaging
built into cloud platform.

00:27:37.530 --> 00:27:42.570
We actually OEM Solus as our
Pub/Sub framework inside us.

00:27:42.570 --> 00:27:45.220
But we also have native
integration services,

00:27:45.220 --> 00:27:46.020
as I said.

00:27:46.020 --> 00:27:48.440
So good, old-fashioned
RESTful services.

00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:49.570
Oh, I shouldn't say--

00:27:49.570 --> 00:27:53.157
Yeah, I guess, RESTfully
is old-fashioned now,

00:27:53.157 --> 00:27:54.490
whenever the next wave comes in.

00:27:54.490 --> 00:27:57.330
But [INAUDIBLE] web services,
et cetera, they're all provided.

00:27:57.330 --> 00:27:59.400
And we have thousands
that you probably know.

00:27:59.400 --> 00:28:02.070
We have these things
called inside SAP core--

00:28:02.070 --> 00:28:04.500
did it get shorter--

00:28:04.500 --> 00:28:07.350
from the point of view
of different services

00:28:07.350 --> 00:28:09.780
invoking our business functions.

00:28:09.780 --> 00:28:13.620
They can now be exposed,
consumed through this layer.

00:28:13.620 --> 00:28:15.840
We have the aspects
of the CoPilot.

00:28:15.840 --> 00:28:18.090
So one of the things
that I want to talk about

00:28:18.090 --> 00:28:22.380
also is, I've shown it here
with the G Suite integrations,

00:28:22.380 --> 00:28:26.160
we actually, for our
SAPPHIRE Session in May,

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:28.140
we announced and
showed how we've

00:28:28.140 --> 00:28:31.350
integrated Sheets,
the first wave,

00:28:31.350 --> 00:28:33.510
into the SAP applications,

00:28:33.510 --> 00:28:36.060
Now, the reason
why I said this is

00:28:36.060 --> 00:28:40.020
like we're trying to
have a single thread

00:28:40.020 --> 00:28:42.270
through to the
integration scenarios.

00:28:42.270 --> 00:28:44.370
So that's the way
we're looking at it.

00:28:44.370 --> 00:28:48.510
And you can see over here
on the extends to the SA S/4

00:28:48.510 --> 00:28:50.600
and their line of
business, i.e.,

00:28:50.600 --> 00:28:52.517
if we're going to create
a conversational bot,

00:28:52.517 --> 00:28:54.725
we don't want to create one
for this application, one

00:28:54.725 --> 00:28:56.880
for that one, [INAUDIBLE]
that application.

00:28:56.880 --> 00:28:58.650
More than development,
it's the fact

00:28:58.650 --> 00:29:02.280
that when we are looking at
the conversational aspects,

00:29:02.280 --> 00:29:06.040
it has to retain the
business context.

00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:08.580
So as the conversation
flows through,

00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:16.350
it can start off in our C/4HANA
hybrids or customer engagement

00:29:16.350 --> 00:29:18.210
scenario, and
could theoretically

00:29:18.210 --> 00:29:22.215
end up in a finance conversation
in our finance system related

00:29:22.215 --> 00:29:23.790
to billing inquiries.

00:29:23.790 --> 00:29:26.540
So because of that, we want
to maintain that context.

00:29:26.540 --> 00:29:29.850
And that's why we have what
we call the SAP CoPilot, which

00:29:29.850 --> 00:29:32.220
now makes use of those
machine learning capabilities

00:29:32.220 --> 00:29:33.810
from our Leonardo functions.

00:29:33.810 --> 00:29:35.730
And those same
Leonardo functions

00:29:35.730 --> 00:29:37.650
is what can now
actually integrate

00:29:37.650 --> 00:29:41.460
into all the Google Brain
and ML and CMLE functions,

00:29:41.460 --> 00:29:42.630
and TensorFlow.

00:29:42.630 --> 00:29:44.670
So that's to give
you a high level

00:29:44.670 --> 00:29:48.400
view of the technical
scenarios that come together.

00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:51.360
And so what I wanted to do
is to talk a little bit more

00:29:51.360 --> 00:29:54.964
about what we've done
in concrete terms.

00:29:54.964 --> 00:29:56.630
Everybody knows it's
all about the data,

00:29:56.630 --> 00:29:59.220
the key areas of govern,
management and enrich,

00:29:59.220 --> 00:30:00.510
and consume.

00:30:00.510 --> 00:30:03.300
So at the end of the day,
I want to explain something

00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:04.720
that I had in the
previous slide.

00:30:04.720 --> 00:30:09.960
So when we look at the consumer
managed aspects, and enrich,

00:30:09.960 --> 00:30:13.990
this is a scenario that's now
been released and it's working.

00:30:13.990 --> 00:30:19.620
This is a way that SAP
S/4HANA can now basically

00:30:19.620 --> 00:30:23.520
interconnect with Google
BigQuery, as well as a Pub/Sub

00:30:23.520 --> 00:30:26.790
frameworks, as well as GCP
machine learning frameworks

00:30:26.790 --> 00:30:30.070
via the cloud storage.

00:30:30.070 --> 00:30:32.580
So in here is SAP
Data Hub, which

00:30:32.580 --> 00:30:36.155
manages the flow of data
and orchestrates that.

00:30:36.155 --> 00:30:38.210
That Data Hub also
now not only just

00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:41.140
pushes data into and
reads from and manages

00:30:41.140 --> 00:30:43.130
your overall orchestration,
but theoretically

00:30:43.130 --> 00:30:45.050
if you are a GCP
user and have already

00:30:45.050 --> 00:30:47.990
made use of extensive
data flows, guess what?

00:30:47.990 --> 00:30:49.730
It's a question of
my previous diagram

00:30:49.730 --> 00:30:51.860
I showed you-- it's about reuse.

00:30:51.860 --> 00:30:54.350
So again, the core
principle here

00:30:54.350 --> 00:30:59.660
is making sure that the
technologies available in GCP

00:30:59.660 --> 00:31:04.400
are now fully integrated into
the business functions of SAP.

00:31:04.400 --> 00:31:07.770
Because the one thing you don't
want to do in SAP, especially

00:31:07.770 --> 00:31:11.150
in general in the RP enterprise
applications, is just

00:31:11.150 --> 00:31:13.040
do database updates.

00:31:13.040 --> 00:31:15.960
It's got to be the
application logic layer.

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:17.650
The other things that
of key importance

00:31:17.650 --> 00:31:19.940
is experience and ease
of use, as I mentioned.

00:31:19.940 --> 00:31:22.460
So from the SAP world,
we've basically released

00:31:22.460 --> 00:31:24.980
and have available
key technologies that

00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:26.840
allow you to do
all these things,

00:31:26.840 --> 00:31:29.270
from the personas,
aspects for people,

00:31:29.270 --> 00:31:31.100
and then the technology--
as I mentioned,

00:31:31.100 --> 00:31:34.980
the machine learning libraries,
as well as REST-based API.

00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:37.910
This is what the Google
team is re-skinning

00:31:37.910 --> 00:31:40.460
via the REST-based APIs
into the business functions

00:31:40.460 --> 00:31:42.137
that we've exposed.

00:31:42.137 --> 00:31:44.720
As well as on the business side,
obviously, the integrations I

00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:47.170
mentioned about, the
G Suite as well as

00:31:47.170 --> 00:31:49.730
tighter integrations
with G Suite

00:31:49.730 --> 00:31:52.460
through those CoPilot functions.

00:31:52.460 --> 00:31:53.240
We have this.

00:31:53.240 --> 00:32:00.020
This is probably not relevant
for GCPers in the crowd,

00:32:00.020 --> 00:32:04.010
but this is part of the
whole suite of solutions

00:32:04.010 --> 00:32:08.030
that comes along for the ride as
part of the SAP Cloud Platform

00:32:08.030 --> 00:32:09.116
to allow you to do things.

00:32:09.116 --> 00:32:10.490
This is where a
lot of the things

00:32:10.490 --> 00:32:12.080
I mentioned before,
there might be

00:32:12.080 --> 00:32:14.050
an overlap within the
specific functions

00:32:14.050 --> 00:32:16.130
that you might be
using GCP to do.

00:32:16.130 --> 00:32:18.710
But again, this is
the SAP-centric view,

00:32:18.710 --> 00:32:22.400
but the point is that you
can now broker these services

00:32:22.400 --> 00:32:25.610
into those external GCP
services without having

00:32:25.610 --> 00:32:31.760
to learn the intricacies
of the SAP context.

00:32:31.760 --> 00:32:33.950
The last one, and
obviously that's

00:32:33.950 --> 00:32:37.130
relevant for most of the
people, these attendees here,

00:32:37.130 --> 00:32:40.400
is looking at the way we
look at machine learning

00:32:40.400 --> 00:32:41.780
and artificial intelligence.

00:32:41.780 --> 00:32:44.250
The key difference
from SAP's world,

00:32:44.250 --> 00:32:46.520
we are a world-leading
technology provider.

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:49.640
And this is what I started
off saying 20 years ago.

00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:52.640
But it's a question
of, our technology was

00:32:52.640 --> 00:32:55.520
developed to power our
business applications.

00:32:55.520 --> 00:32:57.290
At the end of the
day, the technology

00:32:57.290 --> 00:32:59.810
is about the business outcomes.

00:32:59.810 --> 00:33:03.350
Technology is an enabler for us,
we are not a technology company

00:33:03.350 --> 00:33:04.396
by itself.

00:33:04.396 --> 00:33:06.770
It's all about developing the
right technologies to power

00:33:06.770 --> 00:33:09.287
the business application
and the business process.

00:33:09.287 --> 00:33:11.120
And that's why when we
look at this and say,

00:33:11.120 --> 00:33:14.300
the way that SAP
approaches machine learning

00:33:14.300 --> 00:33:17.930
and AI in general, and any
other innovation, new generation

00:33:17.930 --> 00:33:21.050
of innovation technologies,
is with the business context

00:33:21.050 --> 00:33:23.810
in mind, with the business
outcomes that our customers are

00:33:23.810 --> 00:33:24.830
expecting.

00:33:24.830 --> 00:33:27.680
So when I look at this, when
I talk about the machine

00:33:27.680 --> 00:33:30.710
learning, the way that we
have attacked and started

00:33:30.710 --> 00:33:35.600
to consume machine learning, is
to provide that core foundation

00:33:35.600 --> 00:33:36.530
enablement.

00:33:36.530 --> 00:33:38.270
We provide the
industry level context.

00:33:38.270 --> 00:33:40.220
So we're looking at
blockchain, we're

00:33:40.220 --> 00:33:44.190
looking at fraud detection in
the financial services world.

00:33:44.190 --> 00:33:46.430
When we look at
consumer interaction

00:33:46.430 --> 00:33:48.380
in our retail world,
we look at using

00:33:48.380 --> 00:33:51.800
the relevant machine learning
algorithm technologies

00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:52.400
that way.

00:33:52.400 --> 00:33:55.280
Same goes for within the
procurement side, in sourcing.

00:33:55.280 --> 00:33:57.730
So it's the industry context
that's applied by us.

00:33:57.730 --> 00:34:01.430
It's not a generalized
algorithm out there

00:34:01.430 --> 00:34:03.260
in terms of what we
want to look at it.

00:34:03.260 --> 00:34:04.400
And the consuming apps--

00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:08.310
again, our consuming apps are
our business applications.

00:34:08.310 --> 00:34:11.210
So as I mentioned, things such
as in our financial world,

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:13.940
the way that we
apply cash is now

00:34:13.940 --> 00:34:17.429
available via automated scenario
from a machine learning.

00:34:17.429 --> 00:34:21.920
So the apps are our business
applications themselves.

00:34:21.920 --> 00:34:24.080
That's really the
context from our point

00:34:24.080 --> 00:34:27.864
of view, is the consuming apps
are our business applications.

00:34:27.864 --> 00:34:29.780
And then the last one
there is bring your own.

00:34:29.780 --> 00:34:32.449
So we have customers,
we have partners--

00:34:32.449 --> 00:34:34.400
it's definitely got shorter--

00:34:34.400 --> 00:34:36.440
from point of view
have developed

00:34:36.440 --> 00:34:39.020
your own machine
learning algorithms

00:34:39.020 --> 00:34:41.060
and perhaps have
your own models.

00:34:41.060 --> 00:34:44.040
So the way that we've
architected our solution,

00:34:44.040 --> 00:34:46.130
our technology
stack, is the fact

00:34:46.130 --> 00:34:50.940
that you can bring your
own and make use of that.

00:34:50.940 --> 00:34:53.510
So that's the same way that
we had, like I mentioned,

00:34:53.510 --> 00:34:56.360
one of our partners, Deloitte,
bought their own machine

00:34:56.360 --> 00:35:00.200
learning algorithm to model
to do the invoice creation

00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:03.770
from a scanned OC image.

00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:07.610
Looking a little bit at
the details behind this--

00:35:07.610 --> 00:35:12.770
from the fact that we can
now also announce it's HANA 2

00:35:12.770 --> 00:35:15.740
service pack 5, I believe.

00:35:15.740 --> 00:35:19.910
We can do what's called
native TensorFlow serving.

00:35:19.910 --> 00:35:25.130
So what this depicts is the fact
that within my SAP HANA world

00:35:25.130 --> 00:35:28.300
I can make a call
out to TensorFlow,

00:35:28.300 --> 00:35:30.890
pass it the relevant
information,

00:35:30.890 --> 00:35:35.060
and have the inference
engine give me back results.

00:35:35.060 --> 00:35:36.760
And then the other
side of this is

00:35:36.760 --> 00:35:40.060
that we can now, using Data
Hub and all the data management

00:35:40.060 --> 00:35:43.240
tools within SAP HANA,
move the relevant data

00:35:43.240 --> 00:35:47.320
over to GCS, which is cloud
storage, which in turn is now

00:35:47.320 --> 00:35:51.730
used by the CMLE engine
on the Tensor processing

00:35:51.730 --> 00:35:57.250
units, retraining model using
the on-demand compute power

00:35:57.250 --> 00:36:00.620
from the TPUs, and
updating that new model.

00:36:00.620 --> 00:36:04.570
So you can have that nice little
continuous training function

00:36:04.570 --> 00:36:05.110
applied.

00:36:05.110 --> 00:36:08.867
And you can also, obviously,
with this, tune the model as

00:36:08.867 --> 00:36:11.200
and when you need,
depending on that--

00:36:11.200 --> 00:36:13.670
depending on the data
outcomes that you're having.

00:36:13.670 --> 00:36:15.470
And since this is
a dev session, I

00:36:15.470 --> 00:36:18.320
thought I better put a
bit of code in there.

00:36:18.320 --> 00:36:20.505
So this actually
is the code to--

00:36:20.505 --> 00:36:22.130
I don't know if you
can see this here--

00:36:22.130 --> 00:36:24.850
call sys afl and
wrapper procedure.

00:36:24.850 --> 00:36:27.850
The AFL is the application
function library inside HANA.

00:36:27.850 --> 00:36:29.230
So to show you, it is real.

00:36:29.230 --> 00:36:33.250
This is where it's making
that call out to the Tensor

00:36:33.250 --> 00:36:34.300
serving engine.

00:36:34.300 --> 00:36:37.360
And you getting back, as you can
see here, it's doing a predict.

00:36:37.360 --> 00:36:39.820
And what it's doing,
is that this version

00:36:39.820 --> 00:36:43.060
allows you to send in
multiple values or an array

00:36:43.060 --> 00:36:45.580
for prediction.

00:36:45.580 --> 00:36:47.970
Example use cases--
as I mentioned,

00:36:47.970 --> 00:36:51.820
I think this is
going to be key here.

00:36:51.820 --> 00:36:53.650
Sorry, I forgot to mention.

00:36:53.650 --> 00:36:55.810
So before I get into
the example use cases,

00:36:55.810 --> 00:36:57.910
as part of the
partnership, we've

00:36:57.910 --> 00:37:01.375
actually developed brand
new solutions with Google.

00:37:01.375 --> 00:37:05.400
The first of which is a solution
called SAP Data Custodian.

00:37:05.400 --> 00:37:09.670
And as you probably can imagine,
this actually came out of--

00:37:09.670 --> 00:37:13.450
I would say, Google
themselves made it relevant.

00:37:13.450 --> 00:37:17.420
Because in the old
ways you used to deploy

00:37:17.420 --> 00:37:19.690
SAP and other
enterprise applications,

00:37:19.690 --> 00:37:23.200
you would have to deploy
multiple regional instances

00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:27.970
because of the communications,
and the segregation duties,

00:37:27.970 --> 00:37:29.140
and all of those things.

00:37:29.140 --> 00:37:33.580
Now, with Google's high speed
interconnects across the globe,

00:37:33.580 --> 00:37:36.160
you could theoretically have
a single instance scenario.

00:37:36.160 --> 00:37:39.270
But the downside of the single
instance because of the GDPR

00:37:39.270 --> 00:37:42.280
now, is all of who's
got access to what data,

00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:44.030
and why are they
doing it that way?

00:37:44.030 --> 00:37:46.720
So that's the solution that
we actually worked with Google

00:37:46.720 --> 00:37:49.425
using their technology in
terms of access control

00:37:49.425 --> 00:37:52.540
lists and security,
and seeing the logging

00:37:52.540 --> 00:37:55.870
involved at the very lowest
level granular level.

00:37:55.870 --> 00:37:58.920
And what we did is, obviously,
we provided, as I mentioned,

00:37:58.920 --> 00:38:02.060
something that's key to SAP
is, process and governance.

00:38:02.060 --> 00:38:03.760
So we provided the
governance framework

00:38:03.760 --> 00:38:08.090
and the management of that
data flows and data controls.

00:38:08.090 --> 00:38:09.790
It's not only about,
did you look at it?

00:38:09.790 --> 00:38:12.250
I can now tell you, did you
have the right to look at

00:38:12.250 --> 00:38:13.690
it, which is authorizations.

00:38:13.690 --> 00:38:17.530
But did you have the right
usage base for that use?

00:38:17.530 --> 00:38:20.040
Because just because you can
look at a social security

00:38:20.040 --> 00:38:21.640
number because
you're in payroll,

00:38:21.640 --> 00:38:24.146
why are you doing this from
within another function?

00:38:24.146 --> 00:38:26.020
So all of those kind of
governance frameworks

00:38:26.020 --> 00:38:28.760
is what SAP is good, and
that's what we've provided.

00:38:28.760 --> 00:38:31.390
And that's, like I say, I think
you saw that on the keynote

00:38:31.390 --> 00:38:34.360
today with [INAUDIBLE],, the
first iteration was released.

00:38:34.360 --> 00:38:35.360
And we're working on it.

00:38:35.360 --> 00:38:37.780
I'm not sure when the
next release level

00:38:37.780 --> 00:38:41.080
is for the Data Custodian.

00:38:41.080 --> 00:38:45.470
Another use case that I actually
worked with the Google team

00:38:45.470 --> 00:38:49.070
for SAPPHIRE, was to take
a concept of an existing

00:38:49.070 --> 00:38:52.720
SAP-based flow, which is all
about a fashion retail that

00:38:52.720 --> 00:38:56.860
requires high touch
interaction with a customer,

00:38:56.860 --> 00:38:59.800
and seeing if we can now
leverage the machine learning

00:38:59.800 --> 00:39:05.680
algorithms inside the
cloud machine engine

00:39:05.680 --> 00:39:09.670
in real-time to interact
with a store associate.

00:39:09.670 --> 00:39:12.890
So the concept here was
that most marketing engines,

00:39:12.890 --> 00:39:18.010
including SAP's, we can derive
a propensity to buy factor.

00:39:18.010 --> 00:39:20.230
We identify, based
on your interactions

00:39:20.230 --> 00:39:23.590
and your demographics, you
probably have a high propensity

00:39:23.590 --> 00:39:25.690
to buy this particular product.

00:39:25.690 --> 00:39:28.330
The next one we actually
worked with the customer

00:39:28.330 --> 00:39:31.040
was, can I say,
well, which channel

00:39:31.040 --> 00:39:35.380
should I offer this product
to the customer via?

00:39:35.380 --> 00:39:36.340
Who should do it?

00:39:36.340 --> 00:39:37.510
Should it be interactive?

00:39:37.510 --> 00:39:40.200
Should it be via social
media, et cetera?

00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:42.310
So that's where it
became a conversation.

00:39:42.310 --> 00:39:45.100
And what we ended up doing, was
to say that, hey, wouldn't it

00:39:45.100 --> 00:39:48.520
be great if we can
actually find a model that

00:39:48.520 --> 00:39:50.290
allows us to do a prediction.

00:39:50.290 --> 00:39:52.950
And that model that we
actually started with

00:39:52.950 --> 00:39:55.980
is actually the YouTube
recommendation engine.

00:39:55.980 --> 00:39:57.970
So we actually used
that, and we tweaked

00:39:57.970 --> 00:40:01.870
it to create a scenario.

00:40:01.870 --> 00:40:04.915
And this a very short
video that I've got.

00:40:04.915 --> 00:40:07.780
It's to show what
we're going to have.

00:40:07.780 --> 00:40:16.690
Basically, this is the
propensity to buy aspects.

00:40:16.690 --> 00:40:23.350
So the CRM system has created a
list of products and customers,

00:40:23.350 --> 00:40:25.990
and said, hey, this
is what we think.

00:40:25.990 --> 00:40:28.330
Then the scenario
you can see here,

00:40:28.330 --> 00:40:31.000
what we have on the right-hand
side, is say Assign All.

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:34.000
You'll see when I click
on that, it goes out.

00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:35.410
Now, what it's
doing, is actually

00:40:35.410 --> 00:40:41.830
that is a live call that
we did to the CMLE engine,

00:40:41.830 --> 00:40:43.720
where we passed it
and we trained it

00:40:43.720 --> 00:40:46.900
based on the historical
information of the sales

00:40:46.900 --> 00:40:48.100
information.

00:40:48.100 --> 00:40:53.740
And then, also, what we added to
that to make the model better,

00:40:53.740 --> 00:40:58.030
is we actually
added in a function.

00:40:58.030 --> 00:41:01.270
Because our assumption
going in was, generally

00:41:01.270 --> 00:41:04.690
speaking, that an
associate would probably

00:41:04.690 --> 00:41:09.940
have a higher success rate
selling or offering a product

00:41:09.940 --> 00:41:13.180
that they personally think
is really good and they like.

00:41:13.180 --> 00:41:15.540
So what we did is we
incorporated this scenario

00:41:15.540 --> 00:41:17.930
of where the associates were
like, yeah, I like that,

00:41:17.930 --> 00:41:19.270
or I don't like that.

00:41:19.270 --> 00:41:24.580
So we were using that function
now into the training model

00:41:24.580 --> 00:41:26.410
in addition to
just who sold what

00:41:26.410 --> 00:41:29.350
in the past historical scenario,
to arrive at what we're calling

00:41:29.350 --> 00:41:31.060
a seller affinity model.

00:41:31.060 --> 00:41:37.510
And again, the last part of this
integration is, we did that,

00:41:37.510 --> 00:41:41.560
we ran the model, and we're
actually trialing it through,

00:41:41.560 --> 00:41:46.600
and the last part of this is to
leverage the SAP Cloud Leonardo

00:41:46.600 --> 00:41:51.930
Analytics to put that
[INAUDIBLE] my HANA one--

00:41:51.930 --> 00:41:54.220
there's a nice feedback loop.

00:41:54.220 --> 00:41:56.290
We wanted to see if
what we're suggesting,

00:41:56.290 --> 00:41:58.000
our hypothesis, is correct.

00:41:58.000 --> 00:42:00.940
So as we actually
run the scenario,

00:42:00.940 --> 00:42:02.860
we're going to run with
the analytics to say,

00:42:02.860 --> 00:42:08.320
OK, here's all the ML
assigned assignments,

00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:13.150
and here's the assignments
that were fed through as is.

00:42:13.150 --> 00:42:14.680
So that's really
the way that we're

00:42:14.680 --> 00:42:19.270
looking at extending our
capabilities in the workplace.

00:42:22.700 --> 00:42:26.341
This is a conceptual
flow of what we did here,

00:42:26.341 --> 00:42:27.590
just to give you a quick idea.

00:42:27.590 --> 00:42:29.214
And this is where we
are really looking

00:42:29.214 --> 00:42:34.530
at the ML functions being
used in the application tier.

00:42:34.530 --> 00:42:39.080
The thing that we've got planned
for, is as part of those action

00:42:39.080 --> 00:42:42.920
lists that came out from
that affinity model, the fact

00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:45.290
that we have within the
machine learning foundation

00:42:45.290 --> 00:42:47.720
from the Cloud Platform,
you have the ability

00:42:47.720 --> 00:42:49.880
to now do resource leveling.

00:42:49.880 --> 00:42:54.890
You can even factor in
not only sell this product

00:42:54.890 --> 00:42:57.870
to that particular customer,
but you can actually now

00:42:57.870 --> 00:43:02.290
factor in information regarding
profitability and pricing.

00:43:02.290 --> 00:43:04.720
Because we've got access to
all of our retail information

00:43:04.720 --> 00:43:07.510
and inventory information
inside Leonardo,

00:43:07.510 --> 00:43:11.180
now I can provide the call
out to the Google engine with

00:43:11.180 --> 00:43:15.550
the additional factors to
improve the model result set

00:43:15.550 --> 00:43:19.600
coming back, i.e., you can
tweak the price of x,y,z,

00:43:19.600 --> 00:43:21.430
because I've got a
lot of this in stock,

00:43:21.430 --> 00:43:25.450
or keep it at full price,
because everybody in social

00:43:25.450 --> 00:43:27.410
media is after the same product.

00:43:27.410 --> 00:43:29.677
So all of those
aspects are built-in,

00:43:29.677 --> 00:43:32.260
but we haven't exposed that yet,
because that's a business use

00:43:32.260 --> 00:43:33.090
case.

00:43:33.090 --> 00:43:37.750
That's really the power of what
our cloud platform is doing

00:43:37.750 --> 00:43:41.980
versus just the native call
straight out to the Google ML

00:43:41.980 --> 00:43:42.580
engine.

00:43:42.580 --> 00:43:45.079
Because we can now provide that
business context right there

00:43:45.079 --> 00:43:46.504
in Insight.

00:43:46.504 --> 00:43:47.920
And again, since
I mentioned, this

00:43:47.920 --> 00:43:50.029
is the actual
Python that's making

00:43:50.029 --> 00:43:51.070
the call to that session.

00:43:51.070 --> 00:43:53.350
Because I did say
it's a dev session.

00:43:53.350 --> 00:43:55.120
The other one that I
wanted to highlight

00:43:55.120 --> 00:43:58.210
was, we have a solution called
the S&amp;P Product Information

00:43:58.210 --> 00:43:59.260
Network.

00:43:59.260 --> 00:44:02.800
And it's about having
all the material,

00:44:02.800 --> 00:44:06.580
master data attributes about
consumer of consumer goods.

00:44:06.580 --> 00:44:08.650
And we created this
scenario to say,

00:44:08.650 --> 00:44:12.370
who's got the best, most
likely image library out there

00:44:12.370 --> 00:44:13.330
right now?

00:44:13.330 --> 00:44:16.810
And who actually exposes
that image library

00:44:16.810 --> 00:44:19.750
through an open API
called Vision API--

00:44:19.750 --> 00:44:20.770
it's Google.

00:44:20.770 --> 00:44:24.730
So in this scenario we wanted
to say, oh, I like that chair,

00:44:24.730 --> 00:44:26.120
take a picture of it.

00:44:26.120 --> 00:44:29.650
And I know that people like
Amazon does it right now,

00:44:29.650 --> 00:44:33.070
and it gives you, oh, it's a
chair, here all the chairs.

00:44:33.070 --> 00:44:36.210
But what we did was
to find it now matched

00:44:36.210 --> 00:44:38.860
that view, extracted
the attributes,

00:44:38.860 --> 00:44:41.440
and then matched it on our
Productive Information Network

00:44:41.440 --> 00:44:43.990
to find actual, real
life attributes,

00:44:43.990 --> 00:44:49.180
like the fact that it's got the
color, the texture, the cloth

00:44:49.180 --> 00:44:50.510
material, et cetera.

00:44:50.510 --> 00:44:52.720
So it was matching at the
business attribute level

00:44:52.720 --> 00:44:54.730
from our Product
Information Network.

00:44:54.730 --> 00:44:58.220
And that's what this
area looks like.

00:44:58.220 --> 00:45:01.810
So as you can see here, we're
using quite a few capabilities

00:45:01.810 --> 00:45:05.680
from the backend
SAP GCP systems.

00:45:05.680 --> 00:45:08.570
But again, from
our point of view,

00:45:08.570 --> 00:45:11.050
it's not about just the
machine learning functions

00:45:11.050 --> 00:45:13.834
that occur out in the
field, it is making sure

00:45:13.834 --> 00:45:15.250
that we provide
the right business

00:45:15.250 --> 00:45:20.110
context for the
consumption and then

00:45:20.110 --> 00:45:22.910
the business processes
behind it as well.

00:45:22.910 --> 00:45:25.060
So that was just to give
you a brief overview

00:45:25.060 --> 00:45:28.120
of the key capabilities
and what we've done.

00:45:28.120 --> 00:45:33.070
And I've got, in
the slides, ideas

00:45:33.070 --> 00:45:35.380
about where to go and do this.

00:45:35.380 --> 00:45:39.130
Downstairs, on level
one, SAP booth,

00:45:39.130 --> 00:45:42.274
there are a couple
of hands-on tutorials

00:45:42.274 --> 00:45:43.690
where you can
actually play around

00:45:43.690 --> 00:45:49.540
with deploying HANA on GCP,
making use of the Android SDK

00:45:49.540 --> 00:45:50.870
aspects as well.

00:45:50.870 --> 00:45:52.780
So some of those are all there.

00:45:52.780 --> 00:45:57.700
And I wanted to know, because
this is near drinking time,

00:45:57.700 --> 00:46:02.000
I want to leave some
time for Q&amp;A aspects.

00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:05.650
So I'm free to take any
questions, because, like I

00:46:05.650 --> 00:46:07.525
said, this was introductory.

